-- title:
--   Dart stabiliser order is half the unit count of the conjugated meet order
-- statement:
--   Fix rationals $a,b$ and a prime $q'$ such that `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q'` holds, i.e. $a<0$, $b<0$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ the algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ has all nonzero elements invertible exactly when $q'$ lies in $v$. Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and $R$ a $\mathbb Z$-submodule of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ which is Eichler of level $N$, i.e. $R=\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_2$ for maximal orders $\Lambda_1,\Lambda_2$ with the relative index of $R$ in $\Lambda_1$ equal to $N$. Let $r$ be a prime with $r\neq q'$ and $r\nmid N$, and let $v$ be a height-one prime containing $r$. Let $n$ be a unit of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}$ (finite adeles) lying in `primeHeckeSet R r`, that is, $n$ lies in the finite adelic box of $R$, $r\,n^{-1}$ lies in that box, while $n^{-1}$ and $r^{-1}n$ do not; assume moreover that $n$ normalises the meet order $S=R\cap nRn^{-1}$, in the sense that `conjByFiniteIdele` of $S$ by $n$ equals $S$. Let $z$ be a further adelic unit whose component at every height-one prime $w\neq v$ is $1$. Consider the graph `graph R v` at the $v$-component $n_v$ of $n$, on the vertex set $(\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v)^\times/\mathrm{level}\,R\,v$ (the level being generated by the local box units of $R$ at $v$ together with the scalar units), with $x$ adjacent to $y$ iff $x\neq y$ and, for some $g$ and some $k$ in the level, one of $x,y$ is the class of $g$ and the other the class of $gkn_v$. Let $d$ be a dart of this graph with first vertex the class of $z_v$ and second vertex the class of $z_vn_v$. Then the stabiliser of $d$ in `ProjAwayUnits R v`, the group of units of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ whose image in $(\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_w)^\times$ lies in the subgroup generated by the local box units of $R$ at $w$ for every $w\neq v$, modulo the kernel of its action on the vertex set, is finite, and its cardinality equals the number of $u\in\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ that are units of the conjugate $z S z^{-1}$ (i.e. $u$ lies in `conjByFiniteIdele (meetOrder R n) z` together with a two-sided inverse in that submodule), divided by $2$ in the natural numbers.
--
--   This is the width dictionary underlying the Čerednik–Drinfeld description of the quotient graph: the stabiliser of a dart in the projective away-unit group has order equal to half the unit count of the left order attached to the corresponding class, matching the weights $\ell(\bar d)$ in Kurihara's and Jordan–Livné's treatment of the Mumford uniformisation. It feeds the identifications of the vertex and edge quotients of the coset graph with class sets of $R$ and of its meet order.
